      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Ii–V–I",
      "body": "The progression **ii–V–I** (2–5–1) steps toward home in two moves, each root a perfect 5th above the next. In C major it is Dm, G, C.\n\n**Why it matters:** It is the most important progression in jazz, and it ends a lot of soul and pop phrases too. Hear it and you know home is coming.",
